WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.046 --> 00:00:10.454
The next day when Ally got to work, Ray was in the office, punching numbers into a small machine.

2
00:00:10.455 --> 00:00:15.990
Ally looked over his shoulder. "You made a mistake."

3
00:00:15.991 --> 00:00:21.476
Ray glanced at a photo of a woman on the desk and sighed.

4
00:00:21.477 --> 00:00:24.425
"I've made more than one mistake."

5
00:00:24.426 --> 00:00:34.187
"I mean your calculations. The total should be 9,789, not 7,989."

6
00:00:34.188 --> 00:00:38.079
"Wow," Ray said. "You're good at math!"

7
00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:42.554
He entered the numbers into his machine again and then shook his head sadly.

8
00:00:42.555 --> 00:00:48.675
"You're also correct. Which means I'm even further in the red than I thought."

9
00:00:48.676 --> 00:00:51.192
"What's wrong with red?" Ally asked.

10
00:00:51.193 --> 00:00:57.083
"It's one of my favorite colors! I mean, I look better in blue and purple, but . . ."

11
00:00:57.084 --> 00:01:00.141
Her words trailed off when Ray shook his head.

12
00:01:00.142 --> 00:01:04.663
"'In the red' means you're losing money or not making a profit.

13
00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:11.541
It's bad news, Ally. I can't keep the diner open much longer."

14
00:01:11.542 --> 00:01:14.194
*** Later Ally wiped down the counters, thinking

15
00:01:14.195 --> 00:01:17.103
hard. There had to be a way to help Ray save his

16
00:01:17.104 --> 00:01:20.662
diner. But she couldn't get money for Ray—she needed too much of it

17
00:01:20.663 --> 00:01:25.770
herself. Another problem was that she knew so little about how things worked on this planet.

18
00:01:25.771 --> 00:01:28.481
"Wait a minute," she reminded herself.

19
00:01:28.482 --> 00:01:34.786
"You're an Astralian. And Astralians solve huge problems in the universe.

20
00:01:34.787 --> 00:01:40.442
There has to be a way to use your Astral mind to keep one tiny diner open."

21
00:01:40.443 --> 00:01:45.151
Just then an old woman using a cane entered.

22
00:01:45.152 --> 00:01:47.926
"I'll help you to a booth," Ally said.

23
00:01:47.927 --> 00:01:55.686
"Aren't you sweet," the old woman said.

24
00:01:55.687 --> 00:02:02.012
Ally got her settled and brought her a cup of tea.

25
00:02:02.013 --> 00:02:07.466
Next Phil, the museum security guard, came in.

26
00:02:07.467 --> 00:02:14.114
"Coffee and an egg sandwich, over easy, with salsa and lettuce, right?" Ally asked.

27
00:02:14.115 --> 00:02:20.844
"Yes!" Phil looked impressed. "You've only worked here for three days, and you remember my order.

28
00:02:20.845 --> 00:02:25.756
But I have to take it to go today. It's going to be busy at the museum.

29
00:02:25.757 --> 00:02:31.738
A local professor, Dr. Cosmo Lloyd, is giving a lecture on alien sightings."

30
00:02:31.739 --> 00:02:36.349
Ally gulped. "Alien sightings?"

31
00:02:36.350 --> 00:02:43.263
"Not real ones." Phil laughed. "Although some people think aliens are real.

32
00:02:43.264 --> 00:02:48.414
You know how the tourists and UFO fans are—they want to believe in life on other planets.

33
00:02:48.415 --> 00:02:50.934
I say it's all nonsense."

34
00:02:50.935 --> 00:02:54.792
Ally forced a smile. "Crazy, right?"

35
00:02:54.793 --> 00:03:02.501
"Oh, miss!" The old woman was waving to her. "I have a question."

36
00:03:02.502 --> 00:03:07.368
Ally gave Phil's order to Ray and then went to the woman's table. "Yes?"

37
00:03:07.369 --> 00:03:15.840
"I can't decide—scrambled eggs or pancakes. Which is better here?"

38
00:03:15.841 --> 00:03:21.361
"They're both delicious. How about we give you half orders of each?"

39
00:03:21.362 --> 00:03:27.728
"That sounds perfect!" the old woman said. "You've solved my problem!"

40
00:03:27.729 --> 00:03:39.552
Ally gave a nervous laugh. "I've . . . um . . . got a special talent for solving problems."

41
00:03:39.553 --> 00:03:41.952
That afternoon Mateo came in for lunch.

42
00:03:41.953 --> 00:03:45.131
He was wearing a T-shirt that Ally hadn't seen before.

43
00:03:45.132 --> 00:03:47.246
"Nice shirt," she said.

44
00:03:47.247 --> 00:03:54.457
"Thanks, it's one of my favorites. You can see all the details of Alpha Centauri."

45
00:03:54.458 --> 00:03:59.451
"That's not Alpha Centauri," Ally said. "That's Beta Burgana."

46
00:03:59.452 --> 00:04:03.475
"Beta Burgana?" Mateo laughed.

47
00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:09.052
"That sounds like the name of a fancy burger, doesn't it, Papi?"

48
00:04:09.053 --> 00:04:14.587
"If we don't get more customers, there won't be any burgers," Ray grumbled.

49
00:04:14.588 --> 00:04:19.244
"We'll think of a way to save the diner. Right, Ally?" Mateo said.

50
00:04:19.245 --> 00:04:24.250
"Absolutely!" Ally sounded more confident than she felt.

51
00:04:24.251 --> 00:04:32.759
When the old woman finished her meal, Ally helped her out the door.

52
00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:36.319
"Have a great day, and come back to see us again." "Oh,

53
00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:44.440
I will!" The old woman winked. "I definitely will." "Well,

54
00:04:44.441 --> 00:04:50.414
that's one more loyal customer," Ally thought. ***

55
00:04:50.415 --> 00:04:59.263
A short while later, Bethany and Kate came in and sat down at the counter near Mateo.

56
00:04:59.264 --> 00:05:05.343
Bethany grinned. "I have the same T-shirt."

57
00:05:05.344 --> 00:05:12.079
"Really?" Mateo blushed. "Are you into science fiction too?"

58
00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:17.602
"It's like all she ever thinks about," Kate said without looking away from her comm device.

59
00:05:17.603 --> 00:05:25.436
Bethany laughed nervously. "Well, it's not the only thing."

60
00:05:25.437 --> 00:05:34.190
Ally wasn't trying to read Bethany's mind, but the girl's thoughts suddenly blared in her ear.

61
00:05:34.191 --> 00:05:40.106
"That's right," Ally blurted out. "Bethany also thinks about Mateo all the time!"

62
00:05:40.107 --> 00:05:42.541
"Oh my gosh!" Kate said.

63
00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:46.523
Mateo and Bethany both turned bright red.

64
00:05:46.524 --> 00:05:53.486
Then Bethany grabbed Kate's hand and pulled her out of the diner.

65
00:05:53.487 --> 00:05:59.247
"Ally!" Mateo shouted after the girls were gone. "I can't believe you said that!"

66
00:05:59.248 --> 00:06:05.850
Ally blinked at him. "But it was true! And I was trying to do another good deed and help you!"

67
00:06:05.851 --> 00:06:10.468
"Help me?" Mateo stared at her in disbelief.

68
00:06:10.469 --> 00:06:23.598
"That's not called help—it's called ruining everything!" He stormed out of the diner.

